<html xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word">
<head><meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8"><title>BuyOnline readme</title></head>
<body style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif">
<h1>BuyOnline - Readme</h1>
<p>Student: NAME, ID</p>

<h2>URL</h2>
<p>http://localhost/lab/project01/buyonline.html</p>

<h2>Files</h2>
<p><b>Pages:</b> buyonline.html, register.html, login.html, mlogin.html, listing.html, buying.html, processing.html, logout.html</p>
<p><b>Style:</b> project.css</p>
<p><b>JavaScript:</b> ajax.js (XMLHttpRequest helpers), register.js, login.js, mlogin.js, listing.js, buying.js, processing.js, logout.js</p>
<p><b>PHP:</b> common.php (shared helpers), check.php, register.php, login.php, mlogin.php, listing.php, catalog.php, buying.php, processing.php, logout.php</p>
<p><b>XSLT:</b> catalog.xsl, processing.xsl</p>
<p><b>Data folder:</b> customer.xml, goods.xml, manager.txt, .htaccess (blocks direct access to the data files)</p>
<p><b>Documents:</b> readme.doc, checklist.doc</p>

<h2>Setup</h2>
<ol>
<li>The data folder is inside project1. The path to it is one line at the top of common.php.</li>
<li>The web server must be able to write to the data folder and its XML files (chmod 777 data, chmod 666 on the files).</li>
<li>PHP needs the SimpleXML, DOM and XSL extensions.</li>
</ol>

<h2>How to use</h2>
<p><b>New customer:</b> open buyonline.html, choose Customer Registration, fill in the form, then use Back.</p>
<p><b>Customer:</b> choose Customer Login. The catalog refreshes every 10 seconds. Add items to the cart, remove them if needed, then press Confirm Purchase or Cancel Purchase. Logout cancels anything still in the cart.</p>
<p><b>Manager:</b> choose Store Manager Login, then Listing to add an item or Processing to see sold items and press Process.</p>

<h2>Manager account</h2>
<p>Admin / 123</p>

<h2>Notes</h2>
<p>Customer passwords are stored in customer.xml as hashes, not plain text. The shopping cart is kept in the PHP session, so it survives a page refresh.</p>
</body>
</html>
